    "created_at": "2016-06-21T12:40:37Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-06-21T12:41:09Z",
    "body": "Good points against an element from both of you.\n\nI don't _think_ we'll need `nomodule2`, but it also seems reasonably harmless to restrict the syntax so that `nomodule`, `nomodule=\"\"`, and probably `nomodule=\"nomodule\"` are the only ways of triggering it, just in case. There could conceivably be other cases where we want to disable scripts based on something vaguely related to modules in the future, so reserving that syntactic space would be nice. \n\nFor example `nomodule=\"wasm\"` seems at least possibly-useful if we ever end up adding `<script type=\"wasm\">`. Although maybe `nowasm` would be nicer in that case.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
