    "created_at": "2017-01-10T15:24:24Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-01-10T15:24:24Z",
    "body": "This looks like optional loading of scripts based on feature detection, exclusively. The fact that we want to check for support for modules is just a case, but it could be anything else at this point.\r\n\r\nTherefore, wouldn't it be better to have a generic solution for including/excluding scripts based on any feature? Something like `supports=\"!modules\"`.",
