    "created_at": "2017-01-11T14:19:58Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-01-11T14:19:58Z",
    "body": "If a browser launches with `type=\"module\"` support but not `nomodule`, it'll download & execute both the module and the bundle. The bundle could be modified to exit early if modules are supported, but the download overhead would be a good enough reason for a developer to avoid `nomodule` until this browser no longer appeared significantly in their stats.\r\n\r\nGiven that, apologies for bikeshedding. Having `nomodule` ship with `type=\"module\"` is way more important than having generic support detection that takes months to work out.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
